      "problem": "Given that $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11),$ construct a statement that also must be true:",
      "worked_solution": "The subtraction property states that\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a-c≡b-c\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can subtract the same integer from both sides of a congruence, keeping the modulus unchanged:\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a-6≡b-6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)\n$$",
